'''Twitter''' is a [[microblogging]] and [[social networking service]] on which users post and interact with messages known as "tweets", owned by American company [[Twitter, Inc.]] [[Registered user]]s can post, like, and retweet tweets, however, unregistered users have the ability to only read tweets that are publicly available. Users interact with Twitter through browser or mobile [[Frontend and backend|frontend]] software, or programmatically via its [[API]]s. Prior to April 2020, services were accessible via [[SMS]].<ref>[https://www.theverge.com/2020/4/27/21238131/twitter-sms-notifications-disabled-jack-dorsey-hack "Twitter turns off its original SMS service in most countries"] Retrieved January 14, 2021.</ref> Tweets were originally restricted to 140 [[character (computing)|characters]], but the limit was doubled to 280 for non-[[CJK characters|CJK languages]] in November 2017.<ref>[https://blog.twitter.com/official/en_us/topics/product/2017/tweetingmadeeasier.html "Tweeting Made Easier"] Retrieved November 7, 2017.</ref> Audio and video tweets remain limited to 140 seconds for most accounts.

Twitter was created by [[Jack Dorsey]], [[Noah Glass]], [[Biz Stone]], and [[Evan Williams (Internet entrepreneur)|Evan Williams]] in March 2006 and launched in July of that year. Twitter, Inc. is based in [[San Francisco, California]] and has more than 25 offices around the world.<ref>[https://about.twitter.com/company "About Twitter"] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160403002854/https://about.twitter.com/company |date=April 3, 2016 }} Retrieved April 24, 2014.</ref> {{As of|2012|alt=By 2012}}, more than 100 million users posted 340 million tweets a day,<ref>{{cite web|url= https://blog.twitter.com/2012/twitter-turns-six |title=Twitter turns six |date=March 21, 2012 |publisher=Twitter}}</ref> and the service handled an average of 1.6 billion [[Web search query|search queries]] per day.<ref name="Twitter_500" /><ref>{{cite web |url=https://blog.twitter.com/2011/engineering-behind-twitter%E2%80%99s-new-search-experience |title=The Engineering Behind Twitter's New Search Experience |date=May 31, 2011 |access-date=June 7, 2014 |work=Twitter Engineering Blog |publisher=Twitter |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140325080255/https://blog.twitter.com/2011/engineering-behind-twitter%E2%80%99s-new-search-experience |archive-date=March 25, 2014 }}</ref><ref>[http://blog.twitter.com/2012/03/twitter-turns-six.html "Twitter turns six"] Twitter.com, March 21, 2012. Retrieved December 18, 2012.</ref> In 2013, it was one of the ten [[List of most popular websites|most-visited websites]] and has been described as "the SMS of the Internet".<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.business-standard.com/india/news/swine-flu%5Cs-tweet-tweet-causes-online-flutter/356604/ |title=Swine Flu's Tweet Tweet Causes Online Flutter |date=April 29, 2009 |first=Leslie |last=D'Monte |work=[[Business Standard]] |quote=Also known as the 'SMS of the internet', Twitter is a free social networking service |access-date=February 4, 2011}}</ref> {{As of|2019||alt= By the start of 2019}}, Twitter had more than 330 million monthly active users.<ref name="Twitter">{{cite news|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/tech/news/2017/10/26/twitter-overcounted-active-users-since-2014-shares-surge/801968001/|title=Twitter overcounted active users since 2014, shares surge on profit hopes|newspaper=USA Today}}</ref> In practice, the vast majority of tweets are written by a minority of users.<ref>Carlson, Nicholas. "[https://www.cbsnews.com/news/stunning-new-numbers-on-who-uses-twitter/ 10% Of Twitter Users Account For 90% Of Twitter Activity]", [[Business Insider]] (June 2, 2009).</ref><ref>Wojcik, Stefan and Hughes, Adam.  "[https://www.pewresearch.org/internet/2019/04/24/sizing-up-twitter-users/ Sizing Up Twitter Users]", [[Pew Research Center]] (April 25, 2019).</ref>

On April 25, 2022, the Twitter board of directors agreed to [[Acquisition of Twitter by Elon Musk|a $44 billion buyout]] by [[Elon Musk]], the CEO of [[SpaceX]] and [[Tesla, Inc.|Tesla]], potentially making it one of the biggest deals to turn a company private.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Isaac |first1=Mike |last2=Hirsch |first2=Lauren |date=April 25, 2022 |title=Musk's deal for Twitter is worth about $44 billion. |language=en-US |work=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2022/04/25/business/elon-musk-twitter/musks-deal-for-twitter-is-worth-about-44-billion?smid=url-copy |access-date=2022-04-26 |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Feiner |first=Lauren |date=April 25, 2022 |title=Twitter accepts Elon Musk's buyout deal |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2022/04/25/twitter-accepts-elon-musks-buyout-deal.html |access-date=April 25, 2022 |website=CNBC |language=en}}</ref>

