'''Twitter, Inc.''' is an American communications company based in [[San Francisco, California]]. The company operates the [[microblogging]] and [[social networking service]] [[Twitter]]. It previously operated the [[Vine (service)|Vine]] short video app and  [[Periscope (service)|Periscope]] livestreaming service.

Twitter was created by [[Jack Dorsey]], [[Noah Glass]], [[Biz Stone]], and [[Evan Williams (Internet entrepreneur)|Evan Williams]] in March 2006 and launched in July of that year. {{As of|2012|alt=By 2012}}, more than 100 million users posted 340 million tweets a day,<ref>{{cite web|url= https://blog.twitter.com/2012/twitter-turns-six |title=Twitter turns six |date=March 21, 2012 |publisher=Twitter}}</ref> and the service handled an average of 1.6 billion [[Web search query|search queries]] per day.<ref name="Twitter_500" /><ref>{{cite web |url=https://blog.twitter.com/2011/engineering-behind-twitter%E2%80%99s-new-search-experience |title=The Engineering Behind Twitter's New Search Experience |date=May 31, 2011 |access-date=June 7, 2014 |work=Twitter Engineering Blog |publisher=Twitter |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140325080255/https://blog.twitter.com/2011/engineering-behind-twitter%E2%80%99s-new-search-experience |archive-date=March 25, 2014 }}</ref><ref>[http://blog.twitter.com/2012/03/twitter-turns-six.html "Twitter turns six"] Twitter.com, March 21, 2012. Retrieved December 18, 2012.</ref> The company went [[Public company|public]] in November 2013. {{As of|2019||alt= By the start of 2019}}, Twitter had more than 330 million monthly active users.<ref name="Twitter">{{cite news|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/tech/news/2017/10/26/twitter-overcounted-active-users-since-2014-shares-surge/801968001/|title=Twitter overcounted active users since 2014, shares surge on profit hopes|newspaper=USA Today}}</ref>

On April 25, 2022, the Twitter board of directors agreed to [[Proposed acquisition of Twitter by Elon Musk|a $44 billion buyout]] by [[Elon Musk]], the CEO of [[SpaceX]] and [[Tesla, Inc.|Tesla]], potentially making it one of the biggest deals to turn a company private.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Isaac |first1=Mike |last2=Hirsch |first2=Lauren |date=2022-04-25 |title=Musk's deal for Twitter is worth about $44 billion. |language=en-US |work=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2022/04/25/business/elon-musk-twitter/musks-deal-for-twitter-is-worth-about-44-billion?smid=url-copy |access-date=2022-04-26 |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Feiner |first=Lauren |date=April 25, 2022 |title=Twitter accepts Elon Musk's buyout deal |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2022/04/25/twitter-accepts-elon-musks-buyout-deal.html |access-date=April 25, 2022 |website=CNBC |language=en}}</ref>

