'''The Boring Company''' ('''TBC''')<ref>{{citation |work= Department of State |publisher= State of Delaware |author= Division of Corporations |title= TBC – The Boring Company|id= 6279803 |date= January 11, 2017 }}</ref><ref name="Chafkin">{{cite web|url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/features/2017-02-16/elon-musk-is-really-boring|title=Elon Musk Is Really Boring|last=Chafkin|first=Max|date=February 16, 2017|publisher=Bloomberg|access-date=February 16, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170216113314/https://www.bloomberg.com/news/features/2017-02-16/elon-musk-is-really-boring|archive-date=February 16, 2017|url-status=live|df=mdy-all}}</ref> is an American infrastructure and [[tunnel construction]] services company founded by [[Elon Musk]]. Its ongoing and proposed projects are designed for intra-city ("loop") transit systems.<ref name=projects2020>{{Cite news|url=https://www.boringcompany.com/projects/|title=The Boring Company Projects page: 2020 |publisher=The Boring Company |date=11 November 2020 |access-date=November 11, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201111175424/https://www.boringcompany.com/projects/|archive-date=November 11, 2020|url-status=live|df=mdy-all}}</ref><ref name=faq2020>{{Cite news|url=https://www.boringcompany.com/faq/|title=The Boring Company FAQ: 2020 |publisher=The Boring Company |date=12 November 2020 |access-date=November 12, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201112053938/https://www.boringcompany.com/faq/|archive-date=November 12, 2020|url-status=live|df=mdy-all}}</ref>

TBC has completed two tunnels in [[Las Vegas]] for loop travel.  It has also completed [[Boring Test Tunnel|one tunnel for testing]] loop travel in [[Los Angeles County]]. Other tunnels are in various stages of discussion and planning.

Musk cited difficulty with Los Angeles traffic, and what he sees as limitations of its two-dimensional transportation network, as his early inspiration for the project.<ref name="Chafkin"/><ref>{{cite web |url=https://gizmodo.com/elon-musk-on-digging-big-ass-tunnel-we-have-no-idea-wh-1791803837 |title=Elon Musk on Digging Big-Ass Tunnel: 'We Have No Idea What We're Doing' |last=Peyser |first=Eve |date=January 30, 2017 |publisher=Gizmodo |access-date=February 17, 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170219045530/http://gizmodo.com/elon-musk-on-digging-big-ass-tunnel-we-have-no-idea-wh-1791803837 |archive-date=February 19, 2017 |url-status=live |df=mdy-all }}</ref> The Boring Company was formed as a [[subsidiary]] of [[SpaceX]], becoming a separate and fully independent company in 2018. As of December 2018, 90% of the [[equity (finance)|equity]] was owned by Musk,<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.theverge.com/2018/12/19/18148061/boring-tunnel-test-drive-hawthorne-tesla-elon-musk |title=I took a ride through Elon Musk's new tunnel in California |date=December 19, 2018 |access-date=December 20, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181220231741/https://www.theverge.com/2018/12/19/18148061/boring-tunnel-test-drive-hawthorne-tesla-elon-musk |archive-date=December 20, 2018 |url-status=live |df=mdy-all }}</ref> with 6% held by SpaceX in return for the use of SpaceX resources during the startup of the company.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/elon-musks-new-boring-co-faced-questions-over-spacex-financial-ties-11545078371 |title=Elon Musk's New Boring Co. Faced Questions Over SpaceX Financial Ties |newspaper=Wall Street Journal |date=December 17, 2018 |access-date=December 18, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181218044810/https://www.wsj.com/articles/elon-musks-new-boring-co-faced-questions-over-spacex-financial-ties-11545078371 |archive-date=December 18, 2018 |url-status=live |df=mdy-all |last1=Copeland |first1=Rob }}</ref> Outside investments during 2019 have changed the equity split.

